      {
        "comment_id": "1790704794",
        "repo_full_name": "expressjs/express",
        "pr_number": 6017,
        "pr_file": "package.json",
        "discussion_id": "1789129519",
        "commented_code": "@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@\n     \"body-parser\": \"^2.0.1\",\n     \"content-disposition\": \"^1.0.0\",\n     \"content-type\": \"~1.0.4\",\n-    \"cookie\": \"0.6.0\",\n+    \"cookie\": \"^0.7.1\",",
        "comment_created_at": "2024-10-07T18:38:48+00:00",
        "comment_author": "NewEraCracker",
        "comment_body": "The applications are under similar organizations. We had this problem before with mismatched dependency versions unless you do the new releases in a very specific order. I have to use npm overrides for other things until they also land.\r\n\r\nPlease keep this change as is with the caret ^. It will make my life easier in the future.\r\nAnother reason is these express dependencies are probably the best I have seen adhering to the semver principles.\r\n\r\nThank you.",
        "pr_file_module": null
      },
      {
        "comment_id": "1790742653",
        "repo_full_name": "expressjs/express",
        "pr_number": 6017,
        "pr_file": "package.json",
        "discussion_id": "1789129519",
        "commented_code": "@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@\n     \"body-parser\": \"^2.0.1\",\n     \"content-disposition\": \"^1.0.0\",\n     \"content-type\": \"~1.0.4\",\n-    \"cookie\": \"0.6.0\",\n+    \"cookie\": \"^0.7.1\",",
        "comment_created_at": "2024-10-07T19:09:42+00:00",
        "comment_author": "joshbuker",
        "comment_body": "Overly strict version pinning (especially in libraries) tends to cause more problems than it solves [in my experience](https://github.com/auth0/ruby-auth0/issues/277).\r\n\r\nAs long as your dependencies are properly adhering to semver ([which sometimes they don't :roll_eyes:](https://github.com/rest-client/rest-client/issues/740)), there should be no downsides to allowing backwards compatible updates with a fuzzy lock ([`^` in npm](https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v8/configuring-npm/package-json#dependencies)).",
        "pr_file_module": null
      },
      {
        "comment_id": "1791588098",
        "repo_full_name": "expressjs/express",
        "pr_number": 6017,
        "pr_file": "package.json",
        "discussion_id": "1789129519",
        "commented_code": "@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@\n     \"body-parser\": \"^2.0.1\",\n     \"content-disposition\": \"^1.0.0\",\n     \"content-type\": \"~1.0.4\",\n-    \"cookie\": \"0.6.0\",\n+    \"cookie\": \"^0.7.1\",",
        "comment_created_at": "2024-10-08T10:03:41+00:00",
        "comment_author": "UlisesGascon",
        "comment_body": "Just to unblock this PR, I will merge my suggested change and move the discussion to https://github.com/expressjs/discussions/issues/279 so we can take a team decision and after that we can do a PR updating all the dependencies with caret if needed :+1:  ",
        "pr_file_module": null
      },
      {
